{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And the meaning of מבכי — a course [of water], and like it נבכי ים." "<b>חבש</b> — it binds up, as: ולא חובשו / לא אהיה חובש." "<b>ותעלומה יוציא אור</b> — what was hidden in the depths of the rivers they will see, when the waters dry up. And the purport of these matters is that the Place [HaShem] does a thing and its opposite — He gives good to the wicked and also repays him evil. Even the places of the earth change: one land yields produce and another land does not grow any grass at all. And to know the essence of these matters — why this is so — man cannot know Tehom. He said: even if man were able to descend to Tehom, he would not find this wisdom, or in the depths of the sea."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:52.630516919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}